Z||000000||Kerri 98||04-15-2001||09:02 PM||||My turn signal fuse keeps blowing, assuming a short somewhere, any tips on where I may begin to look before having to take it in? I am terrified of electrical problems..HAHA...86 Fiero 2M4||||reg||9
Z||000001||FieroJoe||04-15-2001||09:16 PM||||First thing would be to check all the bulbs and wiring around them, just to see if there is anything screwy right there.<P>Does the fuse blow immediatly once you turn the signals on, or does it happen after they have been blinking for a while (i.e at a light).  Does it also blow when you use the hazard flashers?<P>------------------<BR>AIM: Snowboarder0311<BR>87 Coupe 5sp. - big resto in progress<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Kerri 98||04-15-2001||09:22 PM||||Fuse can last a few days, then all of a sudden I notice I have no blinkers. I will need to check the things you told me. The fuse does not blow if I turn on the hazard lights. Will keep you posted.<P><BR>OK, HERES THE SCOOP......<BR>  I got in the car today and drove to the left a bit out of my driveway, then POP went the fuse. At that time, no headlights,signals, etc were on. I'm thinking maybe the short is in the steering column where the turn signal handle is..What are ya'lls opinion before I start disassembling things there. I hate using hand signals, hehe, please help before I get another ticket.<P><BR>[This message has been edited by Kerri 98 (edited 04-15-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by Kerri 98 (edited 04-16-2001).]||||reg||1
